From 1fedd94a0eede7676553eba882ba32bba90273e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:23:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Stop running service work before the emulation shuts down

Tangelo closed 1-3 s after stopping Mario Golf, Badge Arcade or Swapdoodle
(access violation in a worker thread). An HLE service's async section
(RunAsync / RunOnThreadWorker), here http:C waiting for a request that was
still open, finished after the services, kernel and timing were destroyed
and then woke its guest thread.

System::Shutdown now first calls KernelSystem::StopAsyncOperations: async
sections no longer wake guest threads, cancel hooks run, and running
sections get up to 10 s to finish. http:C cancels its requests: a body
still waited for is given up, the connection in use is shut down
(httplib ClientImpl::stop), the progress callback aborts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
